From skeid #29: since the atomic reload (k29 I1) the old state is kept, but the reload error is re-raised into the request that triggered it. With a config file this happens once (mtime moves on); with a config_loader every reloading request gets a 500 until the config is fixed. Fix: log the reload failure (and expose it on admin/health), serve the request with the kept state, back off retries. Test.
